{
  "chapter.2152B0EE8804F761.title": "06 • Astral Sorcery: Read the Sky",
  "task.7403BBBAB0BEDB9B.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.492340992A6EADAC.title": "Start here: Astral Sorcery",
  "quest.492340992A6EADAC.quest_subtitle": "Start Here",
  "quest.492340992A6EADAC.quest_desc": [
    "This Astral Sorcery 2.0 port uses constellation discovery, focal points, staged altars, Liquid Starlight and lumen networks. It differs substantially from older Astral Sorcery tutorials. The bundled Tome is the primary reference for structures and unlocking knowledge.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/astral.png width:330 height:150 align:center}",
    "",
    "&b&lChoose a branch&r",
    "• Discovery",
    "• Crafting & Infusion",
    "• Attunement & Light",
    "• Lumen & Mastery",
    "",
    "Your route: Tome and Astrolabe -> focal-point crafting -> Illuminated and Resonating tables -> Luminous altar and attunement -> lumen and focused starlight -> Iridescent crafting.",
    "",
    "&eStart with the first equipment milestone, then follow the branch you need."
  ],
  "task.570F82C60EE7C55F.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.6537F2A7876A677B.title": "Map legend & completion rules",
  "quest.6537F2A7876A677B.quest_subtitle": "Reference",
  "quest.6537F2A7876A677B.quest_desc": [
    "Follow a branch that solves your next problem. Equipment icons lead to concrete inventory milestones; the book card is a reference, and a large diamond marks a workshop project.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the setup before crafting. Item milestones detect your inventory without consuming items. Their practical checkmarks are optional reminders; final workshop projects require a practical confirmation. An item in your bag does not prove that a machine is configured. Existing equipment counts: do not rebuild a working system just for this map.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "JEI shows this pack's current recipes. Branches explain how the systems connect. Optional side projects are independent of the main route; no casino win is required."
  ],
  "quest.329B06384D220AE6.title": "Open the living Tome",
  "quest.329B06384D220AE6.quest_subtitle": "Discovery",
  "quest.329B06384D220AE6.quest_desc": [
    "The Tome reveals more as your knowledge advances. A dark entry can indicate an unmet discovery or progression condition.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Craft the Tome, open its research chart and read Welcome, Ores and Astrolabe. Follow its connections alongside these quests; use its structure and recipe pages for exact layouts.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "These quests explain the current port. Old instructions involving a different telescope or altar sequence may not apply."
  ],
  "quest.0A5DD29211B6E891.title": "Marble and Aquamarine",
  "quest.0A5DD29211B6E891.quest_subtitle": "Discovery",
  "quest.0A5DD29211B6E891.quest_desc": [
    "Early tools and structures need Astral materials. Aquamarine comes from shale around suitable waters; Marble supplies precise structural blocks.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Find Aquamarine Shale and gather Aquamarine. Collect the mod's Marble and inspect the cut variants in JEI. Keep raw and decorative forms organized for future structure recipes.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A similar white stone from another mod is not a valid substitute for an Astral structure block unless explicitly accepted."
  ],
  "quest.142538FFC0673A1D.title": "Study constellation paper",
  "quest.142538FFC0673A1D.quest_subtitle": "Discovery",
  "quest.142538FFC0673A1D.quest_desc": [
    "A constellation drawing tells you a pattern and its visible moon phases. Reading paper is not the same as discovering the stars.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Find Constellation Paper in exploration loot and study it with right-click. Note its shape and moon phases, then check the matching entry in the Tome.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep a paper reference while observing. If the constellation is absent tonight, check the lunar schedule instead of repeatedly retracing it."
  ],
  "task.64CBA76933310A70.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.62AAFA8076D01B14.title": "Observe through an Astrolabe",
  "quest.62AAFA8076D01B14.quest_subtitle": "Discovery",
  "quest.62AAFA8076D01B14.quest_desc": [
    "The Astrolabe helps discover constellations and locate the focal points used for early crafting.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "At a clear suitable night, look through it. Use the mouse wheel to adjust its angle marker. Hold sneak to trace the paper's constellation connections; release sneak to clear an incorrect attempt.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Also search for a focal-point light column and look directly at it to record it. Bare patches in the grass can help you find candidate locations."
  ],
  "task.452A34257426BE34.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3FC719625D2AAD38.title": "Find your focal point",
  "quest.3FC719625D2AAD38.quest_subtitle": "Discovery",
  "quest.3FC719625D2AAD38.quest_desc": [
    "A focal point concentrates a constellation's light onto a world column. It is a location, not a block you craft and carry.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Locate and mark a focal point using the Astrolabe at night. Clear a small working area there and keep its sky access open. Confirm its position before dropping recipe ingredients.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep item collectors and magnets away while doing ground transformations; disturbing the recipe pile can stop the process."
  ],
  "quest.62B3F6E1E3B71A8E.title": "Make the Resonating Wand",
  "quest.62B3F6E1E3B71A8E.quest_subtitle": "Discovery",
  "quest.62B3F6E1E3B71A8E.quest_desc": [
    "The Wand starts starlight devices, reveals missing structure pieces and helps locate buried Rock Crystal Ore.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the Tome's Wand recipe. Place its ingredients together on open ground at your focal point and let the transformation finish. Collect the Wand and test its structure-preview interaction later.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use the current recipe page for quantities. Do not try to craft this port's Wand by copying an old workbench recipe."
  ],
  "quest.41196F16F623D4D8.title": "Find a Rock Crystal",
  "quest.41196F16F623D4D8.quest_subtitle": "Discovery",
  "quest.41196F16F623D4D8.quest_desc": [
    "Rock Crystals have individual properties and support several later systems. They are not all equally valuable.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use the Wand's response to search deep underground. Mine the ore yourself with a suitable pick and collect the crystal nearby. Read its properties before choosing how to use it.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The bundled Tome warns that crystals released without a nearby player can be lost. Save a good specimen instead of using it as your first disposable catalyst."
  ],
  "task.688357CF11E01AE0.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0CEBE470008B5F33.title": "Illuminated Crafting Table",
  "quest.0CEBE470008B5F33.quest_subtitle": "Discovery",
  "quest.0CEBE470008B5F33.quest_desc": [
    "Your first Astral table is made by a focal-point transformation and unlocks further knowledge when obtained.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Follow the Tome recipe to transform a crafting table with the required materials at a focal point. Place the result, arrange a supported recipe and activate it with the Wand at night.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "This first table needs no surrounding multiblock. Do not build a later altar structure around it to compensate for an incorrect recipe."
  ],
  "task.604C80EC71C6BA8D.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.422823A2345D74FF.title": "Draw Liquid Starlight",
  "quest.422823A2345D74FF.quest_subtitle": "Crafting & Infusion",
  "quest.422823A2345D74FF.quest_desc": [
    "The Lightwell extracts liquid from a catalyst. Liquid Starlight becomes a recurring crafting and infrastructure resource.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place a Lightwell with clear space above. Add Aquamarine or a crystal and collect Liquid Starlight when enough accumulates. Keep a modest reserve for your first upgrades.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The catalyst cannot be recovered and eventually breaks. A block above the basin destroys it; pipes can draw from below."
  ],
  "quest.3EBCB8FDC0B1D518.title": "Use starlight transformations",
  "quest.3EBCB8FDC0B1D518.quest_subtitle": "Crafting & Infusion",
  "quest.3EBCB8FDC0B1D518.quest_desc": [
    "Starmetal and other transformed materials connect early focal-point work to later tools and altars.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the Tome's Starmetal instructions and current JEI transformations. Produce the required material through a supported route, then inspect Stardust and Chisel uses.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not infer every transformation from an item's name. Check the recipe type: table, focal point and infusion are different processes."
  ],
  "task.2AAE5DBBA833A5ED.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2E04B992EDF7CAE9.title": "Relay ingredients",
  "quest.2E04B992EDF7CAE9.quest_subtitle": "Crafting & Infusion",
  "quest.2E04B992EDF7CAE9.quest_desc": [
    "Focus Relays hold ingredients outside the table grid. Their physical placement lets an altar find them.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Make relays and place them according to the next altar's structure page. Right-click to place an item; use an empty hand to retrieve it. Keep the air above each relay clear.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Relays are not linked with the Linking Tool. Position matters; their stored ingredients appear in the altar interface."
  ],
  "task.7FF2F70BB41FD99E.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.41EC1C221A41A935.title": "Resonating table upgrade",
  "quest.41EC1C221A41A935.quest_subtitle": "Crafting & Infusion",
  "quest.41EC1C221A41A935.quest_desc": [
    "This upgrade replaces the first table in place and requires a surrounding structure before it can work.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Prepare the upgrade recipe, Liquid Starlight and the indicated marble/relay structure. Perform the nighttime upgrade, then use the Wand to reveal any missing structure pieces.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "THREE CHECKS: First read the altar tier required by the recipe. Next verify its exact marble and relay structure with the Wand preview. Finally check time/sky and the item placements. More relays do not compensate for the wrong altar tier.",
    "",
    "THIS PORT: The installed 2.x sequence is Illuminated -> Resonating -> Luminous -> Iridescent. The names, focal points and lumen system differ from many older videos; use the installed Tome for the actual structure drawing.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Start with the smaller required layout. Later recipes can demand the expanded outer ring and additional ingredients."
  ],
  "task.2626ADC5ED0687FE.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.765A95C8D7785933.title": "Infusion and a chalice",
  "quest.765A95C8D7785933.quest_subtitle": "Crafting & Infusion",
  "quest.765A95C8D7785933.quest_desc": [
    "The Starlight Infuser uses a structure and surrounding liquid pools to transform materials. A chalice can supply liquid and spare the pools.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build the exact Tome layout, fill every required pool, place a supported input and activate with the Wand. Refill consumed liquid between crafts, or configure a nearby Containment Chalice.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The Infuser works day or night; missing liquid or structure blocks will not be fixed by waiting for midnight."
  ],
  "task.28B7C444D3436231.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.1BD6E00F6CC87805.title": "Luminous Crafting Altar",
  "quest.1BD6E00F6CC87805.quest_subtitle": "Crafting & Infusion",
  "quest.1BD6E00F6CC87805.quest_desc": [
    "The Luminous tier expands the structure again and introduces a constellation-focus slot for later recipes.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Follow the upgrade page: prepare the outer relays, ground ingredients and nearby chalices before starting. Finish the larger structure and inspect the focus slot in the new altar.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Some later recipes consume an attuned focus crystal. Read that requirement before using your best crystal."
  ],
  "task.33C78D4579E27037.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.19A8EA75AB2C1D69.title": "Attune yourself",
  "quest.19A8EA75AB2C1D69.quest_subtitle": "Attunement & Light",
  "quest.19A8EA75AB2C1D69.quest_desc": [
    "Attunement opens a constellation's perk path. The altar is a separate structure from your crafting altar.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build the open-sky plaza shown in the Tome. At night, hold the correct paper to place relays in its pattern. Once the discovered constellation is visible and the pattern lights, stand on the altar without sneaking.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Read the available paths before choosing. Attunement is not something to change casually with an unfamiliar reset item."
  ],
  "task.7E82CFE521BD447B.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.214EFBFC84DD00A8.title": "Attune a crystal",
  "quest.214EFBFC84DD00A8.quest_subtitle": "Attunement & Light",
  "quest.214EFBFC84DD00A8.quest_desc": [
    "An attuned crystal carries a constellation identity for altar recipes and focused-starlight equipment.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "With the attunement pattern active under the correct constellation, drop a Rock or Celestial Crystal onto the altar. Retrieve and inspect the resulting attuned crystal.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Label or separate crystals by constellation. A valid crystal with the wrong attunement still cannot satisfy a recipe that asks for another focus."
  ],
  "task.175D846542F50902.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.76F0829EBB40EC66.title": "Produce your first lumen",
  "quest.76F0829EBB40EC66.quest_subtitle": "Lumen & Mastery",
  "quest.76F0829EBB40EC66.quest_desc": [
    "Lumen is typed magical energy derived from Liquid Starlight and constellation flowers. Each array becomes associated with its produced type.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Fill a Lumen Array with Liquid Starlight, add a suitable flower catalyst and watch its reserve grow. Build separate arrays for different types rather than trying to switch one repeatedly.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Arrays need neither sky nor a multiblock. They slow near empty/full reserves; redstone stops production but does not make the catalyst permanent."
  ],
  "task.689649FA12081504.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3D0E870194144E90.title": "Move and bind lumen",
  "quest.3D0E870194144E90.quest_subtitle": "Lumen & Mastery",
  "quest.3D0E870194144E90.quest_desc": [
    "Generating lumen is only useful when a consumer can receive the required type. Filaments form the distribution network.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the Tome's filament and binding pages, connect one producer to one supported consumer and demonstrate an effect or stored amount changing. Then inspect the Lumen Crystallizer and binding recipes.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "KEEP SYSTEMS DISTINCT: Liquid Starlight is a stored fluid. Lumen uses arrays and filaments. Focused starlight uses an attuned focus and Linking Tool under a matching constellation. A pipe carrying the first cannot replace either of the other two.",
    "",
    "ONE CONSUMER TEST: Label the producer with its type, connect the shortest valid link and watch a single consumer. Extend only after consumption is visible. A network with many unverified links is much harder to diagnose.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Prove one short connection before building a web. Compare resource type, reach and consumer requirements when nothing flows.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/astral.png width:330 height:150 align:center}"
  ],
  "task.7EF0183F13EC99A5.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7F6D201DD011DABA.title": "Focused starlight",
  "quest.7F6D201DD011DABA.quest_subtitle": "Attunement & Light",
  "quest.7F6D201DD011DABA.quest_desc": [
    "A Starlight Focus Crystal supplies a constellation's starlight when it sits in a matching focal-point column.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Make a focus from an appropriately attuned crystal, place it at a matching focal point with sky access, and use the Linking Tool to link a nearby valid target with clear line of sight.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The constellation must be present for its flow. Multiple links share output; this network is different from lumen filaments."
  ],
  "task.5A0183FAC1C5EBE8.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.597437B03E959B34.title": "Combine lumen aspects",
  "quest.597437B03E959B34.quest_subtitle": "Lumen & Mastery",
  "quest.597437B03E959B34.quest_desc": [
    "Alchemy Arrays combine nearby aspects into higher-tier lumen for stronger bindings and advanced crafting.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Choose one second-rank lumen recipe in the Tome. Place the feeding arrays within direct reach and line of sight, provide starlight and the correct catalyst, then confirm the combined output.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Filaments do not supply an Alchemy Array's recipe inputs in this port; its source arrays must be nearby directly."
  ],
  "task.00382111575E6B42.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2E7D2E5692E2083C.title": "Iridescent crafting",
  "quest.2E7D2E5692E2083C.quest_subtitle": "Lumen & Mastery",
  "quest.2E7D2E5692E2083C.quest_desc": [
    "The final altar upgrade brings together liquid, lumen, focused starlight and a constellation focus.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the full upgrade recipe before beginning. Prepare the required five basic lumen types, Armara starlight and focus, ground materials and chalices. Complete the larger structure and upgrade at night.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "PREPARE FOUR INVENTORIES: Item ingredients, Liquid Starlight, the required lumen aspects and the correctly attuned focus/starlight supply. Read whether the focus is consumed before dedicating your best crystal.",
    "",
    "CHECKPOINT: Complete the Wand structure preview before waiting for the correct night. Then observe one ingredient transfer or consumption event at a time. If the ritual stops, identify which resource stopped changing rather than rebuilding the entire altar.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The upgrade consumes its focus. Diagnose the four systems separately: structure, item ingredients, liquid and magical supply."
  ],
  "task.49065D39557691BD.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.05DF96953BD401F0.title": "Choose a useful reward",
  "quest.05DF96953BD401F0.quest_subtitle": "Lumen & Mastery",
  "quest.05DF96953BD401F0.quest_desc": [
    "Late Astral progression offers tools, movement, enchantment support and stronger bindings. Choose something that serves your play style.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the Iridescent Tools, Resplendent Prism and movement-wand pages. Craft one useful upgrade and test its actual ability in a small controlled area.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Tool areas and special attacks can be larger than a normal action. Learn their controls before using them near your base."
  ],
  "task.51604B60C71F2C24.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.79DFA6E51292A76D.title": "Project: a mapped observatory",
  "quest.79DFA6E51292A76D.quest_subtitle": "Lumen & Mastery",
  "quest.79DFA6E51292A76D.quest_desc": [
    "An observatory is maintainable when its focal points, constellations and resource networks are identifiable.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Label your focal points and arrays, store paper references and backup catalysts, and complete one advanced recipe without guessing which system supplies it. Explain how you would restore it after a shortage.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use the Tome's live unlocks as the final authority. These guide tasks do not grant Astral research or bypass its discoveries."
  ],
  "task.1F9014CA03D9FF8E.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3C0BAC272E0E96DF.title": "Stone that fits the structure",
  "quest.3C0BAC272E0E96DF.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Discovery",
  "quest.3C0BAC272E0E96DF.quest_desc": [
    "Astral structures distinguish raw, engraved, chiseled, pillar and other marble forms. A white block in the right position is not sufficient if its variant is wrong.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Make a small selection of the exact marble variants shown by your next Tome structure, including eight pillars. Store them separately from ordinary building stone and compare their tooltips with the structure preview.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use the Wand to locate incorrect positions. Do not replace every block when the preview highlights just one wrong variant."
  ],
  "task.435C304D290FE235.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.6B6F2A6464B4477B.title": "A reserve of Liquid Starlight",
  "quest.6B6F2A6464B4477B.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Crafting & Infusion",
  "quest.6B6F2A6464B4477B.quest_desc": [
    "Liquid Starlight feeds several later operations. A stable supply begins with the Lightwell and a catalyst, then needs storage that does not interfere with its clear space.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Produce and collect one bucket. Refill the collection setup and observe another production cycle. Keep a reserve for the next upgrade before starting several infusion operations.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The catalyst is consumable. A stopped Lightwell may need a replacement rather than a larger surrounding structure."
  ],
  "task.2CE6313B91CE35FB.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.12BC7DE2C89C489A.title": "Refill the ritual, not the whole altar",
  "quest.12BC7DE2C89C489A.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Crafting & Infusion",
  "quest.12BC7DE2C89C489A.quest_desc": [
    "The Containment Chalice supports Liquid Starlight supply near suitable processes. It helps separate a valid structure from a fluid shortage during repeated crafting.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place it according to the installed Tome, provide Liquid Starlight, and run one supported Infuser operation. Inspect the pool and chalice levels afterward to learn what was consumed and replenished.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A chalice does not provide lumen or constellation starlight. Check which magical resource the recipe actually lists."
  ],
  "task.2ED82F8CDEFFBB72.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7721599BA974CCAC.title": "Keep crystal purposes separate",
  "quest.7721599BA974CCAC.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Discovery",
  "quest.7721599BA974CCAC.quest_desc": [
    "Crystals carry properties and can later carry attunement. Treating every crystal as an interchangeable ingredient makes it easy to consume the one intended for a focus.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Collect two ordinary Rock Crystals, compare their tooltips, and reserve one for progression. Label storage for ordinary, attuned and focus crystals before beginning recipes that consume them.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The inventory goal counts crystals, not their properties. Selecting the appropriate crystal remains a deliberate part of the recipe."
  ],
  "task.1AD8F530470CCFA7.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5FE1EE60CF778BA5.title": "Make the resource visible",
  "quest.5FE1EE60CF778BA5.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Lumen & Mastery",
  "quest.5FE1EE60CF778BA5.quest_desc": [
    "A Lumen Crystal gives you a tangible milestone in the lumen branch. Its production depends on the relevant array, supply and crystallizing process.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the Lumen Crystallizer entry, choose one available aspect and establish its direct supply. Produce one crystal and compare the producer and consumer before and after the craft.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A full producer and idle consumer usually point to the link, resource type or consumer conditions rather than a shortage of catalysts."
  ],
  "task.548E7A1F48D23827.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3D87955B8983E5B3.title": "A link with a purpose",
  "quest.3D87955B8983E5B3.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Attunement & Light",
  "quest.3D87955B8983E5B3.quest_desc": [
    "The Linking Tool belongs to the focused-starlight system. The current port has other magical transport methods, so not every pair of nearby blocks should be linked with it.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use an appropriately attuned focus at a matching focal point and link one valid target with clear line of sight. Check the required constellation and observe that target while the sky conditions are suitable.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Focus Relays for altar ingredients are positioned, not linked this way. Lumen Filaments also belong to a different system."
  ]
}
